.TH NEO-DICTATE 1 "2026-11-14" "gnome-phone 0.1.9" "GNOME Phone"
.SH NAME
neo-dictate \- dictation for GNOME Phone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neo-dictate
.SH DESCRIPTION
Turns speech into text on the phone: the microphone button starts and stops listening, and what is said goes into the
document at its cursor as it is said. Speech is recognised by Moonshine's streaming transcriber on the phone itself,
from the user's default audio source.
.PP
The document is kept in
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/neo-dictate/document.txt .
The application's
.B dictate
action (org.gtk.Actions on /neo/Dictate) starts and stops listening as the button does.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/neo-dictate/libmoonshine.so
Moonshine's library, loaded when listening starts (from the system's library path if it is not there).
.TP
.I /usr/share/neo-dictate/models/
The models, a directory each, named as Moonshine names them (tiny-streaming-en, small-streaming-de, ...); one in
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/neo-dictate/models/
is found first. The smallest streaming model for the user's language is used, else the smallest English one.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MOONSHINE_ORT_SINGLE_THREAD
neo-dictate sets it to 1 unless it is set: Moonshine runs on one thread.
